{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>ונתנו.</b> The second nun has a dagesh because it serves in place of two nuns — וְנָתַנְנוּ." "<b>ואת בנתיכם נקח לנו.</b> You find in the condition that Hamor stated to Jacob, and in the reply of Jacob's sons to Hamor, that they pinned the preference upon Jacob's sons — to take the daughters of Shechem whichever they would choose, and their daughters they would give to them according to their pleasure, as it is written: ״וְנָתַנּוּ אֶת בְּנֹתֵינוּ״ — according to our pleasure; ״וְאֶת בְּנֹתֵיכֶם נִקַּח לָנוּ״ — as many as we desire. But when Hamor and Shechem his son spoke to the inhabitants of their city, they reversed the matter: ״אֶת בְּנֹתָם נִקַּח לָנוּ לְנָשִׁים וְאֶת בְּנֹתֵינוּ נִתֵּן לָהֶם״ — in order to appease them so they would agree to be circumcised."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:06.026431788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}